; Binds `(echo-tag s)` to `:impl "wasm:tag"` — the sibling double.wasm
; exports `tag` as identity on a keyword-tagged value. The arg slot is
; declared `any` because the validator distinguishes `keyword` AST
; nodes (`:foo`) from `symbol` AST nodes (bare names), and `:params`
; only knows the latter — there is no `keyword` ValueType
; (`src/Plugin.zig:260-276`). The result slot is `symbol`: the codec
; carries the value as tag `0x05` (`Value.keyword`), which the
; type-comparison layer labels `"symbol"`
; (`src/wasm_plugin_invoker.zig:230`). Together they pin the §18 §18
; codec round-trip — keyword/string (`0x05` vs `0x04`) distinction
; crosses the boundary intact, no JSON-style `$kw` hack.
(plugin :name double :version "1.0.0"
  (expr-func :name echo-tag
    :arity (fixed 1)
    :params [any]
    :result symbol
    :impl "wasm:tag"))
